Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] outcome watch mark: audit names cron+watch, lazy
 watch read, dated far wake, card titles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up nits from the PR #2049 exact-head reviews (GH 5889672918, 5891307272; card t_01a1d487e7253c82):

1. outcome-audit: a done chat that owns a cron AND watches a card reported only
   done_owns_cron (the watch branch was an `elif`). It now reports every reason that
   applies, joined (`done_owns_cron+done_watching`), with both item lists in `on`, so
   the audit matches the tooltip. Single-reason rows are unchanged.
2. _derive_current read the crons and watches (every board + the cron store) before the
   declared-waiting and card_read_failed returns, which discard them. Both are now read
   after those returns.
3. Desktop wake label: 'Wed 09:00' is ambiguous past a week, so a wake more than 6 days
   out reads 'Wed Nov 25 09:00'.
4. Desktop tooltip leads with the watched card's title: 'verify the re-run limit
   (t_watch1, wakes Wed 09:00)'; an untitled card keeps 't_… (wakes …)'.
5. kanban_watch._read_chat_watches swallowed every sqlite3.Error on the subscriber query,
   so a locked/busy board read silently as "no subscriber watches". It now checks that
   kanban_notify_subs exists and lets other errors reach the caller's guard, which logs
   them (_guarded in the outcome, the audit's warning).

RED -> GREEN: tests/tools/test_kanban_watch_park.py (3 new tests failed before, pass
after; plus a legacy-board test), apps/desktop session-outcome.test.ts (3 failed before)
and session-row-stripe.test.tsx. The desktop tests now pin the clock so the
weekday/date label is deterministic.

